<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Respond</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>respond &lt;message&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>respond Thanks, see you at the bank!
</pre>
<p>Answers the last person who sent you a tell, without your having to type 
their name. It works even when you can't see them: an invisible player or 
an immortal. Be careful: if another tell arrives just before you answer, 
your response goes to that person instead.
</p><p>Like a tell, it can't reach someone who ignores you, or who is busy 
writing a message. (Reply is something else: it answers a message on a 
board; see <a cmd='#'>Help Reply</a>.)
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Tell</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ignore</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Reply</a>
</pre>




</div>